    92	## 2. Part (1): the invariant, and what it is invariant under
    93	
    94	### 2.1 `n_min` is well defined, and the profile is the invariant part
    95	
    96	For `psi in Aut(C^2)`, `psi o F` is Keller (`Jac(psi o F) = (Jac psi o F)·Jac F in
    97	C^*`), noninvertible, of the same geometric degree `N`, and
    98	`A_{psi o F} = psi(A_F)`; the source curve is literally unchanged,
    99	`(psi o F)^{-1}(A_{psi o F}) = F^{-1}(A_F) = E`. So
   100	
   101	> **DEFINITION.** `n_min(F) := min{ deg closure(psi(A_F)) : psi in Aut(C^2) }`.
   102	
   103	A nonempty set of positive integers has a least element: `n_min` is well defined,
   104	and is an invariant of the target-`Aut` class of `F`. This is the campaign's
   105	promoted `d_min` discipline (`D1-DEGREE`, CNA §1.4;
   106	`b0-reducible-n5-opus5-20260831.md:417-419`), and the raw-degree refutation is
   107	already banked as **THEOREM NO-DEG-CAP `[D]`**
   108	(`reducible-all-n-opus5-20260901.md:335-343`, `T(x,y) = (x,y+x^k)`). The grok
   109	ideation item (d) reproduces that argument: **CONFIRMED**, and **not new**. What
   110	is new below is what replaces it.
   111	
   112	Everything the downstream gates use is `Aut`-invariant: the singularity types of
   113	`A_F` and their `delta_p`, `r_p`, the branch structure, `k`, `nu`, `beta`; and
   114	`a`, `a_p`, `W`, `s_l`, `mu_l`, `K_p`, which are defined from `F` and the covering
   115	and are untouched by `psi`. Not invariant: `n = deg A_F-bar`, `delta_infty`,
   116	Chau's `(m,d,e)`, `max(deg P, deg Q)`.
   117	
   118	### 2.2 THEOREM SG-INV: the semigroup at infinity, and `#gaps = delta_aff`
   119	
   120	Under `H2`, `Lemma A` (MI, banked) gives `D~ ≅ A^1`, so `D := A_F` carries a
   121	polynomial parametrisation `t |-> (a(t), b(t))` that is **birational** onto `D`.
   122	Put `S := C[a,b] ⊆ C[t]` and
   123	
   124	```text
   125	   Gamma  :=  { deg_t f(a(t),b(t))  :  f in C[u,v], f not in I(D) }  =  { deg_t g : g in S\{0} }.
   126	```
   127	
   128	> **THEOREM SG-INV.**
   129	> (i) `C[t]` is a finite `S`-module and `Frac(S) = C(t)`; hence `Gamma` is a
   130	>     numerical semigroup (`gcd = 1`, finitely many gaps).
   131	> (ii) `#(N \ Gamma) = dim_C C[t]/S = sum_{p in Sing D} delta_p =: delta_aff`.
   132	> (iii) For every `psi in Aut(C^2)`, `Gamma(psi(D)) = Gamma(D)`.
   133	> (iv) `n := deg closure(D) = max(deg a, deg b) in Gamma`, and
   134	>      `deg_t f(a,b) = sum_{q in A^2} (f · D)_q` — `Gamma` is exactly
   135	>      Abhyankar-Moh's *semigroup at infinity*.
   136	>
   137	> *Proof.* (i) `a` is nonconstant, so `C[t]` is finite over `C[a] ⊆ S`; `S ⊆ C[t]`
   138	> have the same fraction field by birationality and `C[t]` is integrally closed, so
   139	> `C[t]` is the integral closure of `S` and `S` contains a conductor ideal
   140	> `t^c C[t]`; hence `Gamma ⊇ [c,∞)`. (ii) Filtering by degree, a `C`-basis of
   141	> `C[t]/S` is `{t^m : m a gap}`, so `dim_C C[t]/S = #(N\Gamma)`; and `S = C[D]`,
   142	> `C[t] = C[D~]`, so `C[t]/S = ⊕_{p in Sing D} (O~_p/O_p)`, of local dimensions
   143	> `delta_p`. (iii) The parametrisation of `psi(D)` is `psi∘(a,b)`, so its degree set
   144	> is `{deg_t (f∘psi)(a,b)}`, and `f |-> f∘psi` is a bijection of `C[u,v]` carrying
   145	> `I(psi(D))` onto `I(D)`. (iv) `f(a(t),b(t))` is a polynomial whose roots, with
   146	> multiplicity, are the points of `D~` over the affine intersections; a generic
   147	> linear form gives `max(deg a, deg b) = deg closure(D)`. ∎
   148	
   149	**Corollary (the delta-budget is an identity, not a constraint).** For a rational
   150	curve of degree `n`, `delta_aff + delta_infty = p_a(n) = (n-1)(n-2)/2`. The left
   151	side splits into the `Aut`-invariant `delta_aff` and the gauge quantity
   152	`delta_infty`; the right side is a gauge quantity. So the budget
   153	`delta(p,q) + sum_i t_i + delta_infty = p_a(n)` **computes `delta_infty` from
   154	`(n, delta_aff)`**; it constrains nothing invariant. Consequently **CD's
   155	`OPEN[DELTA-INFTY-NOT-NUMERICAL]` is not a blocker** for any consumer that is
   156	rewritten in `delta_aff` (§5 does exactly that).
   157	
   158	**Explicit demonstration of the gauge dependence** (driver `/tmp/degaf/family3.py`,
   159	exact over `Q`):
   160	
   161	```text
   162	  D  = image( t^3 , t^12 + t^4 + t^2 ) :  n = 12,  delta_aff = 3,  delta_infty = 52
   163	  psi = (u,v) |-> (u, v - u^4)         :  n =  4,  delta_aff = 3,  delta_infty =  0
   164	  both:  one ordinary (2,3) cusp at t=0  and exactly k = 2 nodes.
   165	```
   166	
   167	Same curve, same `Gamma`, same `k`; degree and `delta_infty` move by 8 and 52.
