   253	### 3.3 A sharper floor: exact necessary conditions on a minimal gauge
   254	
   255	Let a gauge have coordinate degrees `p <= n` after a linear target change chosen
   256	so that `p := min{ deg_t l(a,b) : l affine-linear }`.
   257	
   258	```text
   259	 (R1) n in Gamma.                                          [SG-INV(iv)]
   260	 (R2) (n, Gamma) satisfies (AM-SG).
   261	 (R3) delta_aff <= p_a(n).                                 [THEOREM DEG-DELTA(a)]
   262	 (R4) there is p in Gamma, 0 < p < n, with p ∤ n and
   263	        delta_aff  <=  p_a(n) - (n-p)(n-p-1)/2 .
   264	```
   265	
   266	`(R4)` is two facts. *First*, the branch of `closure(D)` at its unique point at
   267	infinity has multiplicity exactly `n - p`: in the chart at `[0:0:1]` the branch is
   268	`(X,Z) = (1/b, a/b) = (tau^n·unit, tau^{n-p}·unit)`, so
   269	`mult = min(n, n-p) = n-p`, and a germ of multiplicity `mu` has
   270	`delta >= mu(mu-1)/2`; combine with `delta_infty = p_a(n) - delta_aff`. *Second*,
   271	if `p | n` the target automorphism `(u,v) |-> (v, v - lambda u^{n/p})` strictly
   272	lowers `max(deg a, deg b)`, so the gauge is not minimal.
