   300	## 4. Part (2), second half: MERIDIAN-FLOOR — an `N`-monotone lower bound
   301	
   302	Nothing above involves `N`. Here is the bridge, and it is a floor.
   303	
   304	> **THEOREM MERIDIAN-FLOOR (all `N`, `H2`).** Let `F` be a noninvertible plane
   305	> Keller map of geometric degree `N` with `A_F` irreducible, `a` the covering
   306	> degree over `A_F°`, `W = N - a = sum_l s_l mu_l`, `S = sum_l s_l`. Then for
   307	> **every** gauge, `n = deg closure(A_F)` satisfies
   308	> ```text
   309	>       n  >=  (N - 1) / (W - S)   >=  (N - 1)/(W - 1) ,     hence   n_min >= ceil((N-1)/(W-1)).
   310	> ```
   311	>
   312	> *Proof.* (1) `F : A^2 \ E -> A^2 \ A_F` is finite (proper over the complement of
   313	> the non-properness set, and quasi-finite), étale (`Jac F in C^*`), of degree `N`,
   314	> with connected total space (`A^2` minus a curve). [This is B3E's LEMMA E-ETALE;
   315	> it is re-derived here from the definition of `A_F` and is not consumed from
   316	> B3E.] Hence the monodromy `rho : pi_1(A^2 \ A_F) -> S_N` is **transitive**.
   317	> (2) By Zariski's theorem the inclusion of a generic line `L` induces a surjection
   318	> `pi_1(L \ A_F) ↠ pi_1(A^2 \ A_F)`, so `pi_1(A^2\A_F)` is generated by the
   319	> `#(L ∩ A_F) = n` meridians of a generic line. [The campaign uses this step at
   320	> `b0-reducible-n5-opus5-20260831.md:421-426`.]
   321	> (3) `A_F` is irreducible (`H2`), so all meridians are conjugate, and their common
   322	> image has cycle type `1^a · prod_l mu_l^{s_l}` (MI:694-695): support of size
   323	> `W`, consisting of `S` nontrivial cycles.
   324	> (4) Start from the partition of the `N` sheets into `N` singletons and adjoin the
   325	> generators one at a time. A permutation `sigma` merges, per cycle `c`, at most
   326	> `len(c)` blocks into one, so it decreases the block count by at most
   327	> `sum_c (len(c) - 1) = W - S`. Transitivity requires the count to fall from `N`
   328	> to `1`, so `n · (W - S) >= N - 1`. `S >= 1` gives the stated weaker form. ∎
   329	
   330	Since the statement holds in every gauge it holds for `n_min`. The `N = 5`,
   331	`W = 2` instance of this table is the record's Gate TG
   332	(`b0-reducible-n5:421-426`, `d_min >= 4`); MERIDIAN-FLOOR is its all-`N`,
   333	all-`W` form, and `7.B'` (`mu_l >= 2`, so `S <= W/2` and `W - S >= W/2`) is the
   334	sharpener when `S` is known.
   335	
