   576	of places of `E` at infinity, because Theorem (E) pins `g(E)` exactly: from
   577	`chi_c(E) = 1 - N nu` and `chi_c(E) = 2 - 2g(E) - n_infty(E)` for irreducible `E`,
   578	
   579	```text
   580	      2 g(E)  =  1 + N nu - n_infty(E) .
   581	```
   582	
   583	(Control: at `N=4`, `nu = k`, HF's B3-N4 gives `g = k_odd - 1` and
   584	`n_infty = 3 + 4k - 2k_odd`, and `1 + 4k - (3+4k-2k_odd) = 2k_odd - 2` ✓.) So the
   585	covering cap carries no independent upper bound on anything that grows with `k`;
